.TH HTTP_SOCKET_READ 3
.SH NAME
http_socket_read \- read operation of the input buffer of an HTTP client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.P
.BI "ssize_t http_socket_read(fd_type " fd ", void* " buf ", size_t " len ", buffer* " b ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR http_socket_read ()
is the operation of
.IR h->q.in ,
where the http structure is
.IR b->cookie .
It reads with recv(2) or tls_read(3) and keeps the state of the response up to date: a read of 0 bytes sets the
status HTTP_STATUS_CLOSED, an error other than "try again" sets HTTP_STATUS_ERROR and stores
.I errno
in
.IR response->err ;
in both cases the socket is not watched any more.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of bytes read, 0 at the end of the stream, -1 with errno EAGAIN when there is nothing for now.
.SH SEE ALSO
http_socket(3), http_socket_write(3)
